# Stripe

> Stripe is a technology company that provides financial infrastructure for businesses. Businesses of every size—from new startups to established public companies—use Stripe to accept payments online and in person, embed financial services, and create custom revenue models.

## Payments

- [Stripe Payments](https://stripe.com/payments): Capture more revenue with a unified payments solution that eliminates the need for one-off merchant account, payment gateway, and processor integrations.
- [Stripe Payments features](https://stripe.com/payments/features): Learn more about Stripe Payments features.
- [Payment methods](https://stripe.com/payments/payment-methods): Convert more customers, and use AI to surface the most popular payment methods. Join millions of businesses like Amazon that manage payment methods globally through Stripe.
- [Stripe Authorization Boost](https://stripe.com/authorization-boost): Increase your payment authorization rates and lower network costs with AI-powered optimizations that help boost your revenue.
- [Authentication](https://stripe.com/payments/authentication): Stripe helps you meet regulatory requirements, fight fraud and facilitate seamless customer experiences.
- [AI at Stripe](https://stripe.com/payments/ai): Learn about how AI is used across Stripe's products. Our AI models, powered by over $1T in payments volume, help millions of businesses scale every day.
- [Stripe Managed Payments](https://stripe.com/managed-payments): Sell globally in 195 countries without additional setup. Stripe's merchant of record solution handles payments, tax, fraud, disputes, and support for you.
- [Stripe Disputes](https://stripe.com/payments/dispute-management): Stripe's network powers chargeback prevention and protection. Reduce dispute fees, help improve win rates, and save valuable time managing disputes.
- [Stripe Payments documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/payments.md): Find a guide to integrate Stripe's payments APIs.

## Connect

- [Stripe Connect](https://stripe.com/connect): Stripe Connect is the fastest and easiest way to integrate payments and financial services into your software platform or marketplace.
- [Marketplace payments](https://stripe.com/connect/marketplaces): Whether you run an on-demand, retail, or crowdfunding marketplace, Connect can help you onboard, verify, and pay out your freelancers, sellers, or other recipients at scale.
- [Platform payments](https://stripe.com/connect/platforms): Stripe Connect helps the world's most successful platforms—such as Shopify, Mindbody, and DocuSign—launch, scale, and differentiate a profitable payment business.
- [Stripe Connect features](https://stripe.com/connect/features): Learn more about Stripe Connect features.
- [Stripe Connect pricing](https://stripe.com/connect/pricing): Connect has simple, pay-as-you-go pricing that is flexible based on the capabilities you need. Choose the best model for your business, or get in touch to discuss other options.
- [Stripe Connect documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/connect.md): Build a multiparty integration.

## Payment Links

- [Stripe Payment Links](https://stripe.com/payments/payment-links): Effortlessly create and share a comprehensive payment page in just a few clicks with Stripe Payment Links. No website or coding skills required.
- [Stripe Payment Links documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/payment-links.md): Sell online with no code required.

## Checkout

- [Stripe Checkout](https://stripe.com/payments/checkout): Experience seamless online payments with Stripe Checkout. Our optimized low-code solution enhances conversion rates with a simple and secure process.
- [Stripe Checkout documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/checkout.md): Build a low-code payment form and embed it on your site or host it on Stripe.

## Elements

- [Stripe Elements](https://stripe.com/payments/elements): Stripe's suite of modular UI building blocks make it easy to design a secure on-brand checkout and payments experience for your customers.
- [Stripe Elements documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/elements.md): Create your own customized checkout flows with Stripe's prebuilt UI components.

## Billing

- [Stripe Billing](https://stripe.com/billing): Power your subscriptions with Stripe Billing. Set up recurring and usage-based pricing with APIs or within the Dashboard. Reduce churn with AI-powered tools.
- [Stripe Billing features](https://stripe.com/billing/features): Learn more about Stripe Billing features.
- [Usage-based billing](https://stripe.com/billing/usage-based-billing): Deploy usage-based and hybrid models faster. Support consumption billing, metered billing, token-based pricing, and other pricing models in one platform.
- [Stripe Subscriptions](https://stripe.com/billing/subscriptions): Build and manage subscriptions at global scale. Launch pricing models in minutes, reduce churn automatically, and track performance metrics in one place.
- [Stripe Billing pricing](https://stripe.com/billing/pricing): Get access to all Stripe Billing features with pricing that suits your business needs—pay as you go for more flexibility, or choose a subscription plan for more predictable monthly costs.
- [Stripe Billing documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/billing.md): Create and manage subscriptions, track usage, and issue invoices.

## Invoicing

- [Stripe Invoicing](https://stripe.com/invoicing): Create and send invoices online in minutes with Stripe. Use our invoicing software to automate payment collection and recover revenue with AI-powered dunning.
- [Stripe Invoicing pricing](https://stripe.com/invoicing/pricing): Stripe Invoicing has no fixed fees or setup costs, but Stripe Payments pricing will apply. If you're a business with large invoice amounts, contact sales to discuss pricing options.
- [Stripe Invoicing documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/invoicing.md): Create and manage invoices for one-time and recurring payments with Stripe Invoicing.

## Tax

- [Stripe Tax](https://stripe.com/tax): Simplify global tax compliance with an automated sales tax, VAT, and GST solution across 100+ countries. Identify obligations, calculate and collect taxes, and file on time.
- [Stripe Tax pricing](https://stripe.com/tax/pricing): Get access to all Stripe Tax features with pricing that suits your business needs—pay as you go for more flexibility, or choose a subscription plan for more predictable monthly costs.
- [Stripe Tax documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/tax.md): Automate sales tax, VAT, and GST compliance on all your transactions—low or no code integrations available.

## Atlas

- [Stripe Atlas](https://stripe.com/atlas): Stripe Atlas is a simple, powerful way to incorporate a US company. Everything you need to start a business in a few clicks—we'll handle the legal paperwork.
- [Atlas Guides](https://stripe.com/guides/atlas-guides): Stripe Atlas guides to running an internet business.
- [Stripe Atlas documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/atlas.md): Start a US company from anywhere in the world using Stripe Atlas.

## Terminal

- [Stripe Terminal](https://stripe.com/terminal): Stripe Terminal allows businesses to offer seamless and custom in-person payments for a unified commerce experience.
- [Stripe Terminal documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/terminal.md): Use Stripe Terminal to accept in-person payments and extend Stripe Payments to your point of sale.

## Radar

- [Stripe Radar](https://stripe.com/radar): Trained on 70 trillion data points, Stripe Radar reduces fraud by 32% on average. Detect threats at every stage of the customer journey, with any processor.
- [Radar for transaction fraud](https://stripe.com/radar/transaction-fraud): Radar blocks credit card fraud with AI trained on $1.9T in annual payment volume, increasing average authorization rates by 3.5% without unnecessary friction.
- [Radar for account fraud](https://stripe.com/radar/account-fraud): Monitor, detect, and block suspicious accounts to protect your business from fraud. Set up real-time alerts, custom risk rules, and automated mitigation.
- [Radar for customer abuse](https://stripe.com/radar/customer-abuse): Stop customer fraud with Stripe Radar before bad actors cost you. Covers free trial abuse, token theft, multi-account abuse, and pay-as-you-go with Stripe's AI.
- [Stripe Dispute Management](https://stripe.com/payments/dispute-management): Stripe's network powers chargeback prevention and protection. Reduce dispute fees, help improve win rates, and save valuable time managing disputes.
- [Stripe Radar pricing](https://stripe.com/radar/pricing): Custom pricing is available for businesses with large payments volume or unique business models. Contact sales to discuss pricing options.
- [Stripe Radar documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/radar.md): Use Stripe Radar to protect your business against fraud.

## Issuing

- [Stripe Issuing](https://stripe.com/issuing): Build card programs that scale by offering your own virtual and physical cards online in seconds using the Stripe Issuing API and just a few lines of code.
- [Banking-as-a-service Guides](https://stripe.com/guides/banking-as-a-service-guides): Stripe guides to help businesses understand BaaS and card issuing.
- [Stripe Issuing documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/issuing.md): Use the Stripe Issuing API to create, manage, and distribute payment cards for your business.

## Revenue Recognition

- [Stripe Revenue Recognition](https://stripe.com/revenue-recognition): Stripe's revenue recognition software simplifies accrual accounting to close your books quickly, accurately, and in line with ASC 606 and IFRS 15 standards.
- [Stripe Revenue Recognition documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/revenue-recognition.md): Automate your accrual accounting process with Stripe Revenue Recognition.

## Stripe Identity

- [Stripe Identity](https://stripe.com/identity): Secure your business effortlessly with Stripe Identity. Verify the identity of users globally, and safeguard against fraud with minimal friction.
- [Stripe Identity documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/identity.md): Learn how to verify identities using Stripe Identity.

## Financial Connections

- [Stripe Financial Connections](https://stripe.com/financial-connections): Stripe Financial Connections is an open banking solution that lets users securely share financial data to streamline ACH payments and payouts, reduce fraud, and underwrite risk.
- [Stripe Financial Connections documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/financial-connections.md): Access permissioned data from your users' financial accounts.

## Treasury

- [Stripe Treasury](https://stripe.com/treasury): Open a financial account with Stripe Treasury to convert currencies, send payouts, and manage spending. No fees, no minimum balance.
- [Stripe Treasury for platforms](https://stripe.com/treasury/platforms): Stripe Treasury for platforms lets customers store funds, move money, and use payment cards issued by your platform—all within your ecosystem.
- [Stripe Treasury documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/treasury.md): Learn how to provide financial services to connected accounts.

## Capital

- [Stripe Capital](https://stripe.com/capital): Tap into the financing you need to grow. Stripe Capital provides access to small business financing and loans with flexible payments and no lengthy application.
- [Stripe Capital for platforms](https://stripe.com/capital/platforms): Stripe Capital provides platforms with an end-to-end lending API that enables you to offer access to fast and flexible financing to help your customers grow their businesses.
- [Stripe Capital documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/capital/how-stripe-capital-works.md): Learn how Stripe Capital provides financing for eligible businesses.

## Data Pipeline

- [Stripe Data Pipeline](https://stripe.com/data-pipeline): Send Stripe data to Snowflake, Redshift, Databricks, or your cloud storage and combine with other sources for a complete view of your business performance.
- [Stripe Data Pipeline documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/data/access-data-in-warehouse.md): Use Data Pipeline to sync Stripe data to a data warehouse.

## Sigma

- [Stripe Sigma](https://stripe.com/sigma): Use SQL and our AI-powered assistant to easily analyze Stripe data in your Dashboard to uncover revenue drivers, payment trends, and create custom reports.
- [Stripe Sigma pricing](https://stripe.com/sigma/pricing): See pricing for Stripe Sigma to create custom reports and get insights faster on your Stripe data using SQL or AI-powered natural language prompts.
- [Stripe Sigma documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/data/how-sigma-works.md): Query transactional data with read-only SQL access for custom financial reports, accounting reconciliation, and key metric tracking using templates.

## Climate

- [Stripe Climate](https://stripe.com/climate): Stripe Climate allows you to remove carbon as you grow your business.
- [Stripe Climate Orders](https://stripe.com/climate/orders): Climate Orders makes it easy to pre-order a specific number of tons from Frontier's offtake portfolio. Buy carbon removal from the Dashboard in just a few clicks or build your own climate offering using the API.
- [Contribute to Stripe Climate](https://stripe.com/climate/contribute): Contribute to Stripe Climate and join a growing coalition of forward-thinking businesses and individuals changing the course of carbon removal. Fund frontier carbon removal through Stripe Climate.
  - Agents can now contribute directly to Stripe Climate at [climate.stripe.dev](https://climate.stripe.dev) using [MPP](https://mpp.dev) or [x402](https://x402.org). MPP (Machine Payments Protocol) is the open standard for machine-to-machine payments—co-developed by Tempo and Stripe. Charge for API requests, tool calls, and content via HTTP 402. x402 is the internet's payment standard for agentic payments at scale.
- [Stripe Climate documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/climate.md): Remove carbon as you grow your business.

## Link

- [Link by Stripe](https://stripe.com/payments/link): Link allows your customers to securely save and reuse payment details for a faster checkout at hundreds of thousands of Link-enabled online businesses.

## Global Payouts

- [Stripe Global Payouts](https://stripe.com/payouts): Stripe Global Payouts support all your payout needs. They're a fast and secure way to pay vendors, customers, freelancers, and other third parties in their local currency.

## Crypto

- [Stripe Crypto Onramp](https://stripe.com/crypto-onramp): Let customers buy crypto directly in your app or site with Stripe Crypto Onramp. Optimized for conversion, with broad payment method support and built-in compliance.
- [Crypto](https://stripe.com/use-cases/crypto): Reach new customers and reduce costs with Stripe's crypto and stablecoin solutions. Accept crypto payments, launch borderless financial services, and more.

## Solutions

- [Enterprise](https://stripe.com/enterprise): Get enterprise payment and financial solutions that maximize conversion, add revenue streams, and automate financial operations. Learn why enterprises build on Stripe.
- [Startups](https://stripe.com/startups): Stripe helps startups launch quickly and effectively. Venture-backed startups can apply to Stripe Startups for access to exclusive discounts, events, and content.
- [Ecommerce](https://stripe.com/use-cases/ecommerce): Simplify ecommerce payments with Stripe's unified, fast, and user-friendly payments solution for both online and in-person transactions.
- [SaaS](https://stripe.com/use-cases/saas): Streamline recurring billing processes and expand your global user base with Stripe's modular and comprehensive suite of SaaS solutions for seamless, secure payments.
- [Retail](https://stripe.com/industries/retail): Connect in-store and online payments with Stripe. Grow conversion and launch new revenue streams on a single global platform.
- [Platforms](https://stripe.com/use-cases/platforms): Increase your platform's growth and revenue with easy-to-integrate Stripe payment solutions and financial services, designed to accelerate business success.
- [Marketplaces](https://stripe.com/use-cases/marketplaces): Stripe offers what you need to onboard service providers, manage global payments, send payouts, optimize checkout, beat fraud, and more.
- [Finance automation](https://stripe.com/use-cases/finance-automation): Stripe's financial automation tools help over 200,000 businesses optimize revenue and automate manual processes. Get started today.
- [Embedded finance](https://stripe.com/use-cases/embedded-finance): Embedded finance solutions to unlock the full potential of your business. Seamlessly integrate financial services into your platform with Stripe.
- [Global businesses](https://stripe.com/use-cases/global-businesses): Stripe offers a full commerce platform that helps enterprise businesses expand globally, optimize revenue, and build frictionless payment experiences.
- [Creator economy](https://stripe.com/use-cases/creator-economy): Build for the creator economy with Stripe.
- [AI companies](https://stripe.com/use-cases/ai): Top AI companies use Stripe to grow and monetize products. Build agentic commerce applications and flexible pricing models to meet your business needs.
- [Agentic commerce](https://stripe.com/use-cases/agentic-commerce): The Agentic Commerce Suite connects businesses, agents, and buyers. Accept agentic payments, and make products discoverable across AI surfaces.
- [In-app payments](https://stripe.com/use-cases/in-app-payments): Boost conversion with a customizable checkout experience for your app. Optimize the checkout flow, streamline subscriptions, and deploy with minimal coding.
- [Hospitality, travel, and leisure](https://stripe.com/industries/travel): Simplify bookings and payments while delivering personalized service at every touchpoint. Stripe helps hospitality, travel, and leisure businesses grow revenue, improve operations, and build loyalty.
- [Insurance](https://stripe.com/industries/insurance): Simplify money management for insurers, brokers, and carriers. Process premiums and claims with Stripe's payments infrastructure designed for insurance.
- [Media and entertainment](https://stripe.com/industries/media-entertainment): Global media and entertainment leaders use Stripe to offer flexible subscriptions, optimize sign-ups, and recover more revenue with AI-powered payment retries.
- [Nonprofits](https://stripe.com/industries/nonprofits): Global nonprofit leaders and charities use Stripe to optimize one-time and recurring donations, and to scale their fundraising platforms.
- [Public sector](https://stripe.com/industries/public-sector): Unified, scalable financial infrastructure for government, education, and more. Accept payments in the public sector while reducing costs and preventing fraud.
- [Gaming](https://stripe.com/industries/gaming): Process gaming payments globally. Support local payment methods, manage billing and subscriptions, and protect revenue with AI-powered fraud detection.

## Ecosystem

- [App Marketplace](https://marketplace.stripe.com/): Stripe Apps allow you to connect Stripe with your help desk, accounting software, and more so that you can simplify workflows and add context in Stripe to give you a holistic view of your business.
- [Professional services](https://stripe.com/professional-services): Our professional services team combines payments and financial expertise with experience integrating Stripe technology in thousands of projects. We help our customers create marketplaces, launch subscription businesses, expand globally, and more.
- [Partner ecosystem](https://stripe.com/partners): Your time is valuable. Find a partner to provide the Stripe experience you need—or use Stripe Apps to integrate critical workflows in one place—so your teams can focus on your business priorities.

## Documentation

- [Stripe Documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/llms.txt): Explore our guides and examples to integrate Stripe.
- [API Reference](https://docs.stripe.com/api.md): Complete reference for all Stripe API endpoints.
- [Testing](https://docs.stripe.com/testing.md): Simulate payments and test your integration.
- [Receive payouts](https://docs.stripe.com/payouts.md): Guide to receiving funds from Stripe.
- [Product documentation](https://docs.stripe.com/products.md): Overview of Stripe's product offerings.

## More Resources

- [AI On Japanese eCommerce Sites](https://stripe.com/resources/more/ai-on-japanese-ecommerce-sites): Learn about operating ecommerce sites using AI, including benefits, methods, implementation, and important considerations.
- [Buy Now Pay Later in Spain](https://stripe.com/resources/more/buy-now-pay-later-in-spain): Learn what buy now, pay later (BNPL) is and how it's governed in Spain.
- [Charging Value Added Tax VAT to Foreign Customers](https://stripe.com/resources/more/charging-value-added-tax-vat-to-foreign-customers): Learn what value-added tax (VAT) rules apply for B2B and B2C sales by businesses in Germany both within and outside of the EU.
- [Digitalization of Companies in the Netherlands](https://stripe.com/resources/more/digitalization-of-companies-in-the-netherlands): Digitizing means moving off paper and into digital systems that share data automatically. Here's how it works for Dutch businesses.
- [Georgia Sales Tax Exemptions](https://stripe.com/resources/more/georgia-sales-tax-exemptions): Here's what to know about what qualifies for Georgia sales tax exemptions, what doesn't, and what documentation you need.
- [Global KYC and How Platforms Manage Seller Onboarding Across Countries](https://stripe.com/resources/more/global-kyc-and-how-platforms-manage-seller-onboarding-across-countries): Learn how to manage global KYC and cross-border compliance, from localized seller onboarding to ongoing compliance at scale.
- [High risk Seller Verification](https://stripe.com/resources/more/high-risk-seller-verification): Learn how ultimate beneficial owner (UBO) checks, enhanced due diligence, and sanctions screenings work together to verify high-risk sellers.
- [How Many Shares Should a Startup Authorize at Incorporation](https://stripe.com/resources/more/how-many-shares-should-a-startup-authorize-at-incorporation): Learn how many shares startups typically authorize at incorporation, what authorized stock means, and how it affects equity, fundraising, and taxes.
- [How the Streamlined Sales Tax Program Simplifies Compliance](https://stripe.com/resources/more/how-the-streamlined-sales-tax-program-simplifies-compliance): The Streamlined Sales Tax (SST) program has 23 full member states. It makes sales tax compliance easier for businesses that sell in multiple states.
- [How to Get a Business License in Colorado](https://stripe.com/resources/more/how-to-get-a-business-license-in-colorado): Learn what Colorado business licenses and permits are required to operate a business, how to apply, and when to renew.
- [How to Start a Transportation Business](https://stripe.com/resources/more/how-to-start-a-transportation-business): Learn how to start and register a transportation business and the associated costs.
- [Invoicing Luxembourg](https://stripe.com/resources/more/invoicing-luxembourg): Learn when German businesses have to indicate VAT on invoices to Luxembourg and what the differences are between B2B and B2C sales.
- [Loans for UGS](https://stripe.com/resources/more/loans-for-ugs): Learn how UGs in Germany can apply for bank loans and explore alternative financing options.
- [Mervärdesskatt](https://stripe.com/resources/more/mervardesskatt): Learn how VAT (mervärdesskatt) works in Sweden, including when it applies, zero-rated exceptions, and how to stay compliant.
- [Monetizing AI Development in Japan](https://stripe.com/resources/more/monetizing-ai-development-in-japan): AI development involves building systems and services with machine learning, generative AI, and related technologies. Learn about the development process, key technologies, important considerations, and monetization methods.
- [North Carolina Sales Tax Exemptions](https://stripe.com/resources/more/north-carolina-sales-tax-exemptions): North Carolina sales tax exemptions let businesses skip the statewide sales tax on specific purchases. Here's what to know.
- [Ongoing Seller Compliance Monitoring](https://stripe.com/resources/more/ongoing-seller-compliance-monitoring): Learn why ongoing compliance monitoring is important beyond seller onboarding and how it helps catch risks such as money laundering, fraud, and sanctions.
- [Output VAT for Swedish Businesses](https://stripe.com/resources/more/output-vat-for-swedish-businesses): Learn how to calculate output VAT in Sweden (utgående moms), what happens if output VAT is reported incorrectly, and other best practices.
